# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
harness-artifacts/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# ── data/ is runtime + generated state — ignore the ENTIRE tree ─────────
# Nothing under data/ is source: managed repo clones, per-session worktrees,
# machine-local key material, regenerable DBs (+ their multi-GB backups —
# staging those once orphaned 12 GiB into .git), operator uploads, per-org
# graph DBs, runtime state, session output, launch-timeline traces, and
# scraped conversations. The app recreates the subdirs it needs on first run;
# any fixture that must be tracked lives under tools/, never here. The specific
# data/ rules kept below are redundant with this blanket rule but document
# *why* each category must never be committed.
#
# ONE tracked exception: data/uploads/.gitkeep (force-added). The container
# platform snapshot is a plain checkout mounted read-only at /workspace/repo,
# and the data/uploads bind needs its mount point to EXIST inside that
# read-only tree or runc fails the launch (auto-j3oj3). The keep-file
# materializes the mount point; upload contents themselves stay ignored.
/data/

# Managed project clones + per-session worktrees (workspace_manager)
data/repos/
data/worktrees/

# Project artifacts (licenses, secrets) — layered config-driven mounts
data/artifacts/

# Dashboard session-cookie HMAC key (unlock gate) — machine-local secret
data/dashboard-session.secret

# Private key material — machine-local, MUST NEVER be committed.
#  - data/tls.{crt,key}: the Tailscale Let's Encrypt cert + key uvicorn serves
#    with (issued by `tailscale cert`, renewed by renew-tls-cert.sh).
#  - data/network/: the auto.network tunnel serving delegates — the mode-0600
#    tunnel:serve key files the connector subprocess signs SERVER_HELLO with
#    (see autonomy.network.serve-cert). One key+cert pair per org.
# The broad *.key/*.pem/*.crt catch-alls are a backstop so no key material
# under data/ can ever be added by name.
data/network/
data/tls.crt
data/tls.key
data/*.key
data/*.pem
data/*.crt
# Project image-signing private key (public half is tracked at deploy/cosign.pub
# after operator provisioning; the encrypted private half is CI-secret only).
deploy/cosign.key

# Operator-supplied attachments/screenshots (runtime, not source)
data/uploads/
data/host-uploads/
data/attachments/

# Databases (derived, regenerable)
data/graph.db
data/graph.db-wal
data/graph.db-shm
data/dashboard.db
data/dashboard.db-wal
data/dashboard.db-shm
# Any DB, its wal/shm sidecars, and timestamped backup/snapshot variants
# (graph.db.backup-*, .hourly-*, .pre-txg5-*, .legacy-*, .corrupted-*, etc.).
# The exact names above miss these; staging them as 300MB–2GB blobs is what
# orphaned 12 GiB into .git. Broad globs so no future variant slips through.
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db.*
# Local backup tier (restic source, ~tens of GB) and runtime logs/pids.
data/backups/
data/*.log
data/*.pid
# Session runtime output (container /workspace/output handoff dirs) and
# per-session launch-timeline traces (data/session-traces/) — all runtime.
data/agent-runs/

# Per-workspace image definitions (agents/projects/<name>/Dockerfile + startup.sh).
# These are ORGANIZATION-SPECIFIC infrastructure — enterprise-ng, enterprise-v5,
# scale-harness are Anchore's. They were purged from this repo's public history
# on 2026-08-01 and must not return: this repo is public, and `git add -A` would
# otherwise re-commit them silently. They live on disk only; agents/build.sh
# reads the filesystem, not git, so ignoring them changes nothing about builds.
/agents/projects/

# Beads (Dolt local state — .beads/issues.jsonl IS tracked via git add -f)
.beads/
!.beads/issues.jsonl
!.beads/config.yaml
.dolt/

# Browser profile (contains auth tokens)
.browser_profile/

# Claude Code local settings (machine-specific)
.claude/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.worktrees/
__pycache__/

# Dashboard — generated/downloaded artifacts (regenerated by start-dashboard.sh)
tools/dashboard/tailwindcss
tools/dashboard/static/tailwind.css

data/auth.db
data/auth.db-wal
data/auth.db-shm
data/dispatch.db
data/dispatch.db-wal
data/dispatch.db-shm

# Runtime state snapshots (regenerated each restart)
data/dispatch.state
data/dispatch.state.tmp
data/event_bus.state
data/event_bus.state.tmp
data/resource_monitor.state
data/resource_monitor.state.tmp

# Diag dumps (event_bus snapshots written by /api/diag/eventbus/snapshot)
data/diag/

# Per-org graph DBs — bootstrap-managed, operator-local data
# (graph://d970d946-f95). Reconstructed by `graph org create` /
# the dashboard first-launch bootstrap path.
data/orgs/

# Backup secrets — generated by tools/graph/backup-setup.sh, operator-local
agents/.restic.pw
agents/backup.env

# Local-only Design Studio test DB (auto-tfsc rename was experiments -> design)
data/experiments.db

# Run output dirs
data/agent_runs/
.beads/config.yaml
.beads/issues.jsonl
data/chatgpt/
data/claude/
data/mcp_relay/

# auto-generated by agents/auto-update-image.sh — records the last built
# tool versions, not a source of truth for them (agents/Dockerfile is).
agents/.build-state

# Generated relay viewers: built on demand from their templates.
tools/dashboard/relay_viewer/.build/

tools/dashboard/plugins/mission_control/viewer/.build/
